5. International Standardized Ratio (INR)\>1.5 or partially activated prohemase time (APTT)\>1.5×ULN;
6. The investigator identified clinically significant electrolyte abnormalities;
7. The patient currently has high blood pressure that cannot be controlled by drugs, which is defined as: systolic blood pressure ≥140mmHg and/or diastolic blood pressure ≥90mmHg;
